        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-25T21:23:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think that caching this information gives us any benefits. In order to have both convenience and performance, we can use compile-time expressions. Since AudioChannelLayout is effectively just an `std::variant` of ints, its instances can be `constexpr` constants. For example, in `Utils.h` we can define constants for layouts. We can use the same `#define` for convenience, for example:\n\n```\nstatic constexpr AUDIO_CHANNEL_LAYOUT_MONO \u003d DEFINE_CHANNEL_LAYOUT_MASK(MONO);\n```\n\nSince both this constant and `getChannelCount` are constexprs, all the actual calculations will be carried out during the compilation phase, so no need to cache anything.\n\nIf we want to restrict the remote submix to certain channel layouts, we can also define a constexpr function for that, instead of a runtime set.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 31,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 31,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "bc5d1d6b6c97b84af026481ee5baf7d652aa196d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0e29ad25_229c0138",
        "filename": "audio/aidl/default/remote_submix/StreamRemoteSubmix.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 56,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-25T21:23:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These checks need to be carried out in the stream creator function (see https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/refs/heads/master:hardware/interfaces/audio/aidl/default/Module.cpp;l\u003d123;drc\u003d7346c436e5a11ce08f6a80dcfeb8ef941ca30176), so that an error can be returned properly. We should get into this code only when we sure that the parameters are correct.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 42,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 56,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "bc5d1d6b6c97b84af026481ee5baf7d652aa196d",
